Subject: let a caller reuse the gRNA precomputation across CRT analyses

Applies to Katsevich-Lab/sceptre at SCEPTRE_SHA = 3ba046b86f33e99dee633fbb8704ee8defdb442d
(DESCRIPTION version 0.99.0, `main` as of 2026-08-07; there is no v0.99.0 tag). Applied by
bin/install_sceptre.R before R CMD INSTALL, with no fuzz and no offset search, so bumping the pin
forces this patch to be revisited rather than silently dropped.

Style follows the upstream Air config (air.toml: 4-space indent, 80-char width, one argument per
line), because 0.99.0 was reformatted end to end for Bioconductor.

Why: on the CRT path sceptre fits a logistic regression of perturbation indicator on covariates
once per gRNA target per analysis, and draws the synthetic treatment assignments from the fitted
probabilities. That fit depends on the gRNA-to-cell assignments and the covariate matrix -- never
on the response counts. This pipeline calls run_discovery_analysis() once per (target, replicate)
with only @response_matrix changing, so every replicate after the first refits an identical model.
Unlike @response_precomputations there is no slot to hand it back in through:
`fitted_probabilities` is a local variable in the two CRT workhorse functions.

What it adds:
  - compute_grna_precomputations(sceptre_object, analysis, grna_targets), exported. Fits the model
    once per target, reproducing the workhorses' row space by calling the same
    get_idx_vector_factory() they do rather than reimplementing the indexing.
  - a `grna_precomputations = NULL` argument on run_discovery_analysis() and run_power_check(),
    threaded down through run_sceptre_analysis_high_level() and run_crt_in_memory_v2() to both CRT
    workhorses. It is injected into args_to_pass only on the CRT branch, mirroring how
    synthetic_idxs is injected on the permutation branch, so run_perm_test_in_memory() -- which
    shares the same do.call -- needs no ignored formal.
  - resolve_grna_precomputation() and check_grna_precomputation(), which reuse a supplied fit or
    fall back to fitting.

Three design points worth keeping if this is rebased:

  1. The cache holds *coefficients*, not fitted values. Fitted values are one double per cell,
     which across a large screen and many targets is gigabytes in the caller's session;
     coefficients are ncol(covariate_matrix) doubles. It also makes the cache symmetric with
     @response_precomputations, which stores fitted_coefs. Reconstruction via
     binomial()$linkinv(drop(X %*% coefs)) is bit-identical, not approximate: glm.fit computes the
     fitted.values it returns as linkinv(drop(x %*% start)) from the same vector it returns as
     coefficients, and the offset is zero here. Verified: identical() TRUE, max abs diff 0.
  2. Each entry records `n_cells` alongside the coefficients, and the guard checks it. This is
     load-bearing, not decorative: the two workhorses fit on different cell sets but the same
     covariates, so the coefficient vector has the same length in both and its length alone cannot
     tell a cache built for one path from a cache built for the other.
  3. A target whose covariates are rank deficient within its own cells is omitted from the cache
     with a warning, not stored. glm.fit returns NA for an aliased coefficient while keeping
     fitted.values valid, so reconstructing from it would make every probability NA. Only reachable
     when the control group is the NT cells, since set_analysis_parameters() already rejects a
     globally rank-deficient design.

The calibration check is deliberately not supported: its gRNA group keys are synthetic
undercover-NT names regenerated on every call, so a cache could never hit.

Note what is NOT cached -- crt_index_sampler_fast() still runs on every call, so the synthetic
treatment assignments are redrawn per replicate. Caching those instead would freeze the resampling
distribution across replicates and destroy the CRT null while still producing plausible output.
There is a comment to that effect at both sampler call sites.

Default is NULL everywhere, so unpatched behaviour is unchanged for any caller that does not opt in.
Upstreaming this is wanted but deferred; the plan is in scalable-baking-key.md (untracked), which is
a plan only -- nothing is implemented upstream.

